res, AUROC values, and acceptance probability. The key assumptions underlying these predictions are that the QE AUROC of 0.82 represents a meaningful improvement over baseline approaches, and there are some additional constraints around QE versus selection decisions that I'm factoring in.\n\nNow I'm working through the specific predictions for exp-017, which involves running LLaMA-3.1-8B on the CoNLL-2003 dataset for cross-model validation. I see that this experiment is already in the registry as completed, but I'm predicting what the best-tier results would look like for it. , looking at the registry, exp_017_llama_conll_infer IS done with metrics showing SJ_rho=0.4314, AUROC=0.7039, etc. So this experiment IS done. But the plan still says \"planned\". Let me just provide predictions anyway as requested.\n\nActually wait - I think the user wants me to predict results for ALL planned experiments regardless of whether they've actually been run. The user's instruction says \"对 experiment_plan 中每个 planned 实验展开详细数据\" - so I should generate predictions for exp-017, exp-019, and exp-024.\n\nLet me think about what results would look like under the \"best\" tier for each:\n\n**exp-017 (ner_llama_conll)**: LLaMA-3.1-8B fine-tuned on CoNLL-2003 should show strong cross-model validation with SJ ρ around 0.43-0.45 matching other models, AUROC near 0.78-0.80, and greedy selection performance staying consistent, which would confirm that three model configurations are sufficient for robust quality estimation.\n\n**exp-019 (simple_verifier_baseline)**: A trained verifier using logistic regression on five signals should close the oracle gap by 25-50%, achieving selection F1 well above greedy baseline and demonstrating that the signals themselves contain useful information even though unsupervised aggregation is where the real bottleneck lies.\n\n**exp-024 (claim_audit)**: The numerical consistency audit should resolve any contradictions and confirm all numbers are internally consistent with no major issues that would undermine the core claims.\n\nFor exp-019, I'm calculating what verifier performance would look like if it closed 25-50% of the oracle gap—for NER that translates to an F1 range of 0.677-0.710, and for RE it's 0.449-0.494. Now I'm structuring all these results into the YAML format.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":57930,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":57930},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"593579c2-c96e-448c-8fb3-fc018ee8bb9b","uuid":"6fefefb9-b36e-431e-9745-7a8848f351e2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012nU34w7JKggniPYG4B23NP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: \"Dual contribution fully lands: QE recognized as practical + diagnostic recognized as novel mechanistic insight; trained verifier confirms gap is closable\"\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"ner_llama_conll\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-017\"\n    description: \"LLaMA-3.1-8B fine-tuned on CoNLL-2003, N=8 inference. Cross-model validation for model-agnostic QE claim.\"\n    expected_results:\n      greedy_f1: 0.924\n      oracle_f1: 0.946\n      oracle_headroom_pp: 2.2\n      SJ_rho_full: 0.431\n      FK_rho_full: 0.418\n      LP_rho_full: 0.307\n      EM_rho_full: 0.435\n      VC_rho_full: 0.426\n      SJ_AUROC: 0.792\n      EM_AUROC: 0.804\n      LP_AUROC: 0.761\n      selection_sj_f1: 0.925\n      selection_lp_f1: 0.924\n      selection_vs_greedy_pp: 0.1\n      degeneracy_rate: 0.56\n      structural_beats_surface: true\n      cross_model_rho_delta_vs_qwen: -0.005\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 best 档下，A6 成立：3 model configs 被接受为充分。LLaMA-8B 在 CoNLL 上的\n      表现应与 Qwen3-8B CoNLL (SJ ρ=0.436, AUROC=0.801) 高度一致，因为：(1) CoNLL 是\n      成熟的 NER 数据集，两个 8B 模型经 LoRA 微调后能力相近（greedy F1 均 ~0.92）；\n      (2) 高能力→高退化率(~56%)→极小 selection headroom（~2.2pp），与 Qwen CoNLL 的\n      4.2pp headroom 和 58% 退化率一致；(3) QE 相关性由 population-level 变异驱动，\n      与模型架构无关。cross-model delta < 1pp 的 ρ 差异证明信号有效性是任务属性而非\n      模型属性。Selection ≈ greedy（±0.1pp）因 headroom 本身就极小。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: LLaMA CoNLL QE Metrics (N=8, T=1.0)\"\n        columns: [Signal, ρ_full, τ_full, AUROC, ECE]\n        rows:\n          - [SJ, 0.431, 0.382, 0.792, 0.115]\n          - [FK, 0.418, 0.371, 0.774, 0.107]\n          - [EM, 0.435, 0.387, 0.804, 0.110]\n          - [VC, 0.426, 0.378, 0.789, 0.095]\n          - [LP, 0.307, 0.241, 0.761, 0.131]\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-Model Comparison (CoNLL NER, N=8)\"\n        columns: [Model, SJ_ρ, EM_AUROC, Greedy_F1, Degeneracy_%]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-8B, 0.436, 0.816, 0.912, 58]\n          - [LLaMA-8B, 0.431, 0.804, 0.924, 56]\n          - [Qwen3-4B, 0.422, 0.776, 0.923, 55]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart comparing 5-signal ρ across Qwen3-8B vs LLaMA-8B on CoNLL — visual confirmation of cross-model consistency (all bars within ±0.02)\"\n    analysis: >\n      LLaMA CoNLL 结果确认 QE 信号有效性是模型无关的。SJ ρ=0.431 vs Qwen ρ=0.436\n      (Δ=-0.005, CI crosses zero) 表明信号排名稳定：structural > surface 在两个架构上\n      均成立。EM AUROC 0.804 接近 best-tier 上限 0.82。极高退化率(56%) 解释了为何\n      selection 无法超越 greedy：56% 的实例上所有 N 个样本 F1 相同，无论用什么信号\n      都无法改善。这进一步验证 capability-degeneracy tradeoff——CoNLL 作为\"已解决\"\n      任务（F1>0.92），模型收敛程度极高。\n\n  - name: \"simple_verifier_baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-019\"\n    description: \"Logistic regression trained verifier on 5 signals (SJ, FK, LP, EM, VC) using existing (input, output, F1) data. 5-fold CV on SciERC NER+RE. Tests whether supervised combination closes oracle gap.\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_verifier_selection_f1: 0.692\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.644\n      ner_oracle_f1: 0.776\n      ner_gap_closure_pct: 36.4\n      ner_verifier_vs_greedy_pp: 4.8\n      ner_verifier_auroc: 0.81\n      re_verifier_selection_f1: 0.442\n      re_greedy_f1: 0.404\n      re_oracle_f1: 0.585\n      re_gap_closure_pct: 21.0\n      re_verifier_vs_greedy_pp: 3.8\n      re_verifier_auroc: 0.78\n      best_unsupervised_ner_selection_f1: 0.650\n      best_unsupervised_re_selection_f1: 0.410\n      verifier_vs_best_unsupervised_ner_pp: 4.2\n      verifier_vs_best_unsupervised_re_pp: 3.2\n      top_features_by_weight: [EM, VC, SJ, LP, FK]\n      cv_std_ner: 0.018\n      cv_std_re: 0.024\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 best 档下，A5 成立：trained verifier closes 25-50% of oracle gap。Logistic\n      regression 能达到 ~36% (NER) 和 ~21% (RE) 的 gap closure，原因：\n      (1) 5 个信号之间存在互补信息——exp_016 已证明 SJ-LP pearson=0.57（NER），即约\n      32% 方差不共享，LR 能利用这部分正交信息；\n      (2) EM 在 conditional set 上 ρ=0.36 且 AUROC=0.75，作为 binary discriminator\n      与连续信号(SJ/LP)组合后能捕获\"全对 vs 部分对 vs 全错\"三层结构；\n      (3) NER gap closure 高于 RE 因为 NER 信号整体更强（best ρ=0.38 vs RE 0.35），\n      且 RE 有 40%+ 的 zero-F1 实例使得 LR 在这些实例上退化为随机；\n      (4) 36% closure 对应 +4.8pp over greedy，远超无监督最佳(LP +0.6pp, p=0.39)，\n      证明信号携带信息但无监督聚合方式太弱——这是 Contribution B 的核心论证支柱；\n      (5) RE closure 较低(21%) 因为 binary dominance 问题——45% zero-F1 实例上 verifier\n      也无法从全错样本中选出正确的（不存在正确样本）。但 21% 仍 >> 0%，证明 gap\n      IS closable。CV std ~0.02 表明结果稳定，不是过拟合。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Trained Verifier vs Unsupervised Selection (SciERC, N=8)\"\n        columns: [Method, NER_F1, NER_Δ_greedy, RE_F1, RE_Δ_greedy]\n        rows:\n          - [Greedy (T=0), 0.644, \"—\", 0.404, \"—\"]\n          - [Best Unsupervised (LP), 0.650, +0.6pp, 0.410, +0.6pp]\n          - [Trained Verifier (LR), 0.692, +4.8pp, 0.442, +3.8pp]\n          - [Oracle, 0.776, +13.2pp, 0.585, +18.1pp]\n      - name: \"Table: Oracle Gap Closure Breakdown\"\n        columns: [Task, Oracle_Gap, Verifier_Gain, Closure_%, Remaining_Gap]\n        rows:\n          - [NER, 13.2pp, 4.8pp, 36.4, 63.6]\n          - [RE, 18.1pp, 3.8pp, 21.0, 79.0]\n      - name: \"Table: LR Feature Importance (|coefficient|, normalized)\"\n        columns: [Feature, NER_weight, RE_weight]\n        rows:\n          - [EM, 0.34, 0.38]\n          - [VC, 0.28, 0.26]\n          - [SJ, 0.21, 0.15]\n          - [LP, 0.11, 0.14]\n          - [FK, 0.06, 0.07]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Gap closure waterfall chart: greedy → best unsupervised → trained verifier → oracle, showing the verifier captures 36% of the remaining gap that unsupervised methods cannot access\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: verifier predicted score vs actual F1, showing calibration (expected r² ~0.35 for NER, ~0.20 for RE)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Trained verifier 实验是 best 档的关键区分器。36% NER gap closure 证明：\n      (a) 信号确实携带足够信息来区分样本质量——unsupervised 聚合（取 argmax）是瓶颈；\n      (b) 无监督方法的失败不是因为信号无信息，而是因为 instance-level aggregation\n      （如 LP argmax）无法利用信号间的交互模式；\n      (c) 即使简单 LR 就能获得显著增益，说明更强的 verifier（DeBERTa、reward model）\n      可能进一步缩小 gap。这直接支撑 paper 的 constructive resolution：\n      \"we show WHAT WOULD BE NEEDED\" 不是空话，而是有实验证据的。\n      RE closure 较低但非零(21%) 的原因是 binary dominance——这恰好验证了 Claim 3\n      的 task-complexity boundary：RE 的 zero-F1 实例本身就没有好样本可选，verifier\n      在这些实例上也无能为力，但在非零子集上 closure 接近 35%。\n\n  - name: \"claim_audit\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: \"Systematic cross-chapter numerical consistency audit. Resolve all quantitative contradictions between Discussion, Limitations, Abstract, Introduction and source experiment data.\"\n    expected_results:\n      contradictions_found: 3\n      contradictions_resolved: 3\n      critical_issues: 0\n      minor_corrections_needed: 5\n      table2_consistency: true\n      abstract_numbers_match_source: true\n      discussion_limitations_aligned: true\n      selection_delta_unified: \"+0.2pp (macro F1, p=0.29)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 best 档下，claim audit 应发现少量可修复的不一致但无 critical issues。原因：\n      (1) D116 之后 Table 2 已统一为 macro F1（selection ≈ greedy, +0.2pp, p=0.29），\n      主要矛盾（Discussion \"+0.1pp\" vs Limitations \"+0.4pp\"）已在 framing 更新中修正；\n      (2) 剩余不一致预计来自：早期实验(512 token) vs 1024 token rerun 的数值差异\n      未完全传播到所有章节；exp_012 vs exp_012_rerun_1024 的 voting_conf ρ 差异\n      (0.502→0.379) 可能在某些段落仍引用旧值；\n      (3) 5 项 minor corrections 典型来源：四舍五入不一致（如 \"AUROC 0.75\" vs 实际\n      0.749）、不同 seed 的数值混用、conditional vs full set 标注不清；\n      (4) 无 critical issues 因为核心 claim 的数值（selection ≈ greedy, QE AUROC\n      ~0.75-0.82, degeneracy 21-58%）已通过 3-seed bootstrap 确认，不存在方向性错误。\n      Best 档假设 soundness score 4-5，这要求所有数值可追溯到源实验——audit 确保这一点。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Audit Results Summary\"\n        columns: [Issue_Type, Count, Severity, Resolution]\n        rows:\n          - [Selection delta inconsistency, 1, Medium, \"Unified to +0.2pp (macro F1)\"]\n          - [Stale voting_conf ρ from 512-token run, 1, Medium, \"Updated to 0.379 (1024-token)\"]\n          - [Rounding inconsistency (AUROC), 2, Low, \"Standardized to 3 decimal places\"]\n          - [Conditional vs full set unlabeled, 2, Low, \"Added (full) or (cond) labels\"]\n          - [Seed not specified in claim, 1, Low, \"Added 3-seed mean ± SD\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Audit 在 best 档下是 soundness 保障而非风险。3 个中等问题均已有明确修复路径：\n      selection delta 统一为 bootstrap-confirmed 数值（+0.2pp, p=0.29, d=0.038），\n      voting_conf 统一为 1024-token rerun 数据。无 critical issues 意味着 reviewer\n      在核查数值时不会发现方向性矛盾——这对 soundness score 4-5 是必要条件。\n      Minor corrections（四舍五入、标注规范）不影响结论但体现 rigor。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":57930,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":57930},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"593579c2-c96e-448c-8fb3-fc018ee8bb9b","uuid":"22bcb673-4858-4da5-aa0e-24a00c8be34c"}
